  "prefLabel": "App 203.03 Waiver or Suspension of Rules by Presiding Officer",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "App 203.03 Waiver or Suspension of Rules by Presiding Officer. The presiding officer upon his or her own initiative or upon the motion of any party, shall suspend or waive any requirement or limitation imposed by this chapter upon notice to affected persons when the proposed waiver or suspension appears to be lawful, and would be more likely to promote the fair, accurate and efficient settlement of issues pending before the council than would adhere to a particular rule or procedure.\n\nSource. #7864-A, eff 4-1-03",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/app100-500.html"
